---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const paths=[
{number:'01',title:'I want my savings to grow',copy:'Bring your starting balance, an affordable regular contribution and a rate you have checked. See how much of the future balance comes from your own deposits.',guide:'how-compound-interest-works',guideLabel:'Understand compound interest',tool:'compound-interest',toolLabel:'Project my savings',question:'Try a lower rate as well. Does the saving habit still get you close to the goal?'},
{number:'02',title:'I am saving towards something',copy:'Bring a target, the amount already dedicated to it and a realistic timeframe. For a home, keep the purchase-cost allowance separate from the deposit itself.',guide:'planning-a-home-deposit',guideLabel:'Plan a home-deposit target',tool:'savings-goal',toolLabel:'Find a monthly saving amount',question:'Check the monthly result against the money left after essential bills. Adjust the timeframe if it does not fit.'},
{number:'03',title:'I want to understand my home loan',copy:'Bring the remaining principal, rate, remaining term and any offset balance or extra repayments. Use the same loan assumptions for both scenarios.',guide:'offset-vs-extra-repayments',guideLabel:'Compare offset and extra repayments',tool:'mortgage',toolLabel:'Explore my repayments',question:'Compare interest, payoff time and fees. Money kept in an offset remains separate from the loan in our model.'},
{number:'04',title:'I want a buffer for the unexpected',copy:'Bring your essential monthly expenses, dedicated emergency savings and an affordable monthly contribution. Choose the number of months you want to cover.',guide:'building-an-emergency-fund',guideLabel:'Build an emergency budget',tool:'emergency-fund',toolLabel:'Work out my buffer',question:'Include annual essentials as monthly amounts. Keep an emergency buffer separate from savings already committed to another goal.'}
];
---
<Base title="Start with your money question" description="Choose the right Howloop calculator, gather the inputs, learn the assumptions and compare a second scenario. A practical starting point for Australian money planning.">
<header class="hl-page-head hl-wrap"><div class="hl-breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Start here</div><span class="hl-eyebrow">A CLEAR FIRST STEP</span><h1>Start with a question.<br/>Leave with a next step.</h1><p>You do not need to connect an account. Choose what you are working towards, read the example and try it with your own numbers.</p></header>
<div class="hl-wrap hl-page-main"><div class="hl-start-grid">{paths.map(p=><section class="hl-start-card"><span class="hl-eyebrow">PATH {p.number}</span><h2>{p.title}</h2><p>{p.copy}</p><ol><li><a href={'/learn/'+p.guide}>{p.guideLabel} →</a></li><li><a href={'/calculators/'+p.tool}>{p.toolLabel} →</a></li><li>{p.question}</li></ol></section>)}</div>
<section class="hl-start-check"><div><span class="hl-eyebrow">MAKE THE NUMBER USEFUL</span><h2>A result is the beginning of a plan.</h2><p>A calculator can answer “what happens with these inputs?” It cannot establish whether a bank will approve a loan, whether you qualify for a bonus, or whether a product suits you.</p></div><ol><li><strong>Check the inputs.</strong> Use available savings, an affordable contribution and the correct period. An annual bill divided by 12 becomes a monthly allowance.</li><li><strong>Keep the assumptions.</strong> Howloop uses monthly approximations. Rates, timing, fees and tax can change the outcome. <a href="/methodology">Read the exact model.</a></li><li><strong>Try a second scenario.</strong> Lower the contribution or rate, or allow more time. A useful plan should make the trade-off visible.</li><li><strong>Verify before acting.</strong> Confirm the current terms with the provider. Get appropriately qualified help for decisions about your own circumstances.</li></ol></section>
<section class="hl-library-note"><h2>Choosing a bank rate?</h2><p>Use the <a href="/banks">bank explorer</a> to locate dated public product data. Start with the basic rate and inspect the conditions. Howloop can model supported base rates and balance tiers; it does not assume you earn every bonus. A custom rate is a scenario that stays constant.</p><p><a href="/learn/bonus-interest-conditions">Learn to read the rate conditions →</a></p></section>
<div class="hl-start-foot"><p>Your inputs stay in your browser. Saving a plan on this device is optional. <a href="/privacy">How privacy works</a>.</p><p>Need a different explanation or found a mistake? <a href="/contact">Send feedback</a>.</p></div>
</div></Base>

